The fix is verified and the project builds successfully. Here's a summary:

## Bug Fix Summary

**Bug:** MAC vendor search was case-sensitive — only uppercase hex letters worked (e.g., `00:16:3E`), while lowercase (`00:16:3e`) returned no results.

**Root Cause:** In `VendorDB.java`, the `findVendors(String filter)` method passed the user's filter directly to case-sensitive predicates (`StringContains` and `MacContains`) without normalizing the case. Since MAC addresses in the database are stored in uppercase (via `VendorUtils.clean()` which calls `.toUpperCase()`), lowercase input failed to match.

**Fix:** Added `filter.toUpperCase()` to normalize the search input before passing it to the predicates.

### Changes Made

**`app/src/main/java/com/vrem/wifianalyzer/vendor/model/VendorDB.java`** (line 77):
```java
// Before:
public List<String> findVendors(@NonNull String filter) {
    Predicate<String> predicate =
        PredicateUtils.anyPredicate(new StringContains(filter), new MacContains(filter));
    ...
}

// After:
public List<String> findVendors(@NonNull String filter) {
    String searchFilter = filter.toUpperCase();
    Predicate<String> predicate =
        PredicateUtils.anyPredicate(new StringContains(searchFilter), new MacContains(searchFilter));
    ...
}
```

**`app/src/test/java/com/vrem/wifianalyzer/vendor/model/VendorDBTest.java`** — Added two new test cases:
- `testFindVendorsWithLowercaseMacFilter` — verifies lowercase hex input finds the same vendors as uppercase
- `testFindVendorsWithMixedCaseMacFilter` — verifies mixed-case hex input works correctly
